ROLE: product_realist  VOTE: red
REAL_USE_CASE: No production agentic workload at realistic constrained-token fraction (f≈0.1–0.2) achieves a measurable win; only synthetic high-f (≥0.35–0.60) JSON-heavy streams reach the ≥5% regime, which lies outside the claimed prose-dominated agentic/tool-calling traffic.
OPERATIONAL_SIGNIFICANCE: Microbenchmark-only. L0 is CPU analytic with proxy cost ratio, no wall-clock, no GPU, no real draft/target acceptance; median +1.33% gain (max +3.98%) at the realistic agentic cell (f∈{0.1,0.2}, gap≤0.30) sits below production noise and below the pre-registered 3% honest-negative threshold.
ADOPTION_BARRIER: [Real-time instrumentation to label grammar-constrained vs prose spans; maintenance burden of per-region k tuning versus a single best-tuned fixed k (2–7) that captures ~98% of the gain; prior-art collision with EAGLE/EAGLE-2 dynamic trees and 2024 confidence-adaptive draft-length works that subsume "lengthen in low-entropy regions"; 1–2% median win does not justify code, testing, and ops complexity; L0 lacks GPU wall-clock measurements of real p_constrained, p_prose, and f on production traces]
RATIONALE: EXP-0006 reports "Median gain, realistic agentic cell (f∈{0.1,0.2}, gap≤0.30): +1.33% (max +3.98%)" and "Pre-registered honest-negative trigger FIRED: median realistic-cell gain (1.33%) < the 3% threshold". "The optimal fixed k is small and region-blended: across the grid the best fixed k is almost always 2–7 (mode k=2)... Because realistic traces are prose-dominated (small f), the trace-level throughput is governed by the prose region" (EXP-0006). Prior-art caveat: "EAGLE / EAGLE-2 (dynamic/confidence-driven draft trees)... and explicitly entropy/region-adaptive or confidence-adaptive speculative decoding (several 2024 works adapt draft length to model confidence — which would subsume the 'lengthen in low-entropy regions' idea)" (EXP-0006). No evidence that production agentic traffic reaches f≥0.35; L0 provides no wall-clock, GPU, or real acceptance data. Prompt version v001.
